<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: U.S. firm creates 210 new jobs in Swords, Dublin.</title>
<headline>U.S. firm creates 210 new jobs in Swords, Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's minister for enterprise and employment, Richard Bruton, said on Tuesday that U.S. company FORE Systems, a supplier of networking products, will create 210 new jobs when it opens a new facility in Swords, Dublin.</p>
<p>Bruton said in a statement that the production centre, which will receive support from IDA Ireland, will be based at Swords Business Park.</p>
<p>&quot;The appointment of an Irish manager and recruitment of the first 60 people will commence in December,&quot; Bruton said.</p>
<p>FORE systems is a publicly quoted company on the U.S. NASDAQ Stock Exchange and employs 1,200 people, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
